------------ KeyWin32SOBailOut ----
SOBailOutAllows the file parser to return an error condition.The parser should return from the VwReadStreamFunc function as soon as possible after this function is called.VOID SOBailOut(WORD wError,     HPROC reserved    );



------------ KeyWin32SOBeginTable ----
SOBeginTableStarts a table definition, indicating that the text in subsequent output calls is part of a table.This function must be called between paragraphs and before row and cell formats are specified.VOID SOBeginTable(HPROC reserved    );



------------ KeyWin32SOEndColumnInfo ----
SOEndColumnInfoEnds the definition of column information.The file parser must call this function immediately after setting the column information. This function can only be called from the VwStreamSection function.VOID SOEndColumnInfo(HPROC reserved    );



------------ KeyWin32SOEndFieldInfo ----
SOEndFieldInfoEnds the definition of field information. The file parser must have previously called the SOStartFieldInfo function.The file parser calls this function immediately after setting the field information. This function can only be called from the VwStreamSection function.VOID SOEndFieldInfo(HPROC reserved    );



------------ KeyWin32SOEndFontTable ----
SOEndFontTableEnds the definition of a font table.The file parser must call this function immediately after setting font entries. This function can only be called from the VwStreamSection function.VOID SOEndFontTable(HPROC reserved    );



------------ KeyWin32SOEndPalette ----
SOEndPaletteEnds the definition of a color palette.The file parser calls this function immediately after specifying the last palette entry.VOID SOEndPalette(HPROC reserved    );



------------ KeyWin32SOEndTable ----
SOEndTableEnds a table definition, indicating that the text in subsequent output calls is no longer part of a table.The function must be called after a row break.VOID SOEndTable(HPROC reserved    );



------------ KeyWin32SOEndTabStops ----
SOEndTabStopsEnds the definition of tabs stops for a paragraph.To set tab stops, use the SOPutTabStop function.The file parser calls this function immediately after setting the last tab stop for the paragraph.VOID SOEndTabStops(HPROC reserved    );



------------ KeyWin32SOGetInfo ----
SOGetInfoRetrieves information about a spreadsheet.VOID SOGetInfo(WORD wInfo,     void VWPTR *pInfo,     HPROC reserved    );



------------ KeyWin32SOGetScanLineBuffer ----
SOGetScanLineBufferRetrieves the address of the buffer for storing the current scan line.This function is called from the VwStreamReadFunc function for each scan line produced. This function sets the variable pointed to by ppScanLineData to the address where the scan line data should be built.WORD SOGetScanLineBuffer(VOID VWPTR *ppScanLineData,     HPROC reserved    );



------------ KeyWin32SOPutBitmapHeader ----
SOPutBitmapHeaderOutputs information about a bitmap.VOID SOPutBitmapHeader(PSOBITMAPHEADER pBitmapHeader,     HPROC reserved    );



------------ KeyWin32SOPutBreak ----
SOPutBreakSets a paragraph, cell, record, page, section, or other type of break.In spreadsheet sections, the last cell in a section must have an associated SO_CELLBREAK break before the SO_SECTIONBREAK or SO_EOFBREAK break.In database sections, the last record in a section must have an associated SO_RECORDBREAK break before the SO_SECTIONBREAK or SO_EOFBREAK break.In word processing sections, the last paragraph does not need an SO_PARABREAK break before the SO_SECTIONBREAK or SO_EOFBREAK break.WORD SOPutBreak(WORD wType,     DWORD dwInfo,     HPROC reserved    );



------------ KeyWin32SOPutChar ----
