------------ KeyGTK3gtk_adjustment_get_value ----
gtk_adjustment_get_value 
Gets the current value of the adjustment. Seegtk_adjustment_set_value .
Syntax
Parameters
adjustment    	a GtkAdjustment
Returns
 The current value of the adjustment.

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_adjustment_set_value ----
gtk_adjustment_set_value 
Sets the GtkAdjustment value. The value is clamped to lie between?lower? and ?upper?.Note that for adjustments which are used in a GtkScrollbar, the effectiverange of allowed values goes from ?lower? to?upper? - ?page_size?.
Syntax
Parameters
adjustment    	a GtkAdjustment.
value    	the new value.

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_adjustment_clamp_page ----
gtk_adjustment_clamp_page 
Updates the ?value? property to ensure that the rangebetween lower and upper is in the current page (i.e. between?value? and ?value? + ?page_size?).If the range is larger than the page size, then only the start of it willbe in the current page.A ?changed? signal will be emitted if the value is changed.
Syntax
Parameters
adjustment    	a GtkAdjustment.
lower    	the lower value.
upper    	the upper value.

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_adjustment_changed ----
gtk_adjustment_changed 
Emits a ?changed? signal from the GtkAdjustment.This is typically called by the owner of the GtkAdjustment after it haschanged any of the GtkAdjustment properties other than the value.
Syntax
Parameters
adjustment    	a GtkAdjustment

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_adjustment_value_changed ----
gtk_adjustment_value_changed 
Emits a ?value_changed? signal from the GtkAdjustment.This is typically called by the owner of the GtkAdjustment after it haschanged the ?value? property.
Syntax
Parameters
adjustment    	a GtkAdjustment

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_adjustment_configure ----
gtk_adjustment_configure 
Sets all properties of the adjustment at once.Use this function to avoid multiple emissions of the ?changed?signal. See gtk_adjustment_set_lower  for an alternative wayof compressing multiple emissions of ?changed? into one.
Syntax
Parameters
adjustment    	a GtkAdjustment
value    	the new value
lower    	the new minimum value
upper    	the new maximum value
step_increment    	the new step increment
page_increment    	the new page increment
page_size    	the new page size
Since 2.14

