------------ KeyGTK3gtk_adjustment_set_lower ----
gtk_adjustment_set_lower 
Sets the minimum value of the adjustment.When setting multiple adjustment properties via their individualsetters, multiple ?changed? signals will be emitted. However, sincethe emission of the ?changed? signal is tied to the emission of the?notify? signals of the changed properties, it?s possibleto compress the ?changed? signals into one by callingg_object_freeze_notify  and g_object_thaw_notify  around thecalls to the individual setters.Alternatively, using a single g_object_set  for all the propertiesto change, or using gtk_adjustment_configure  has the same effectof compressing ?changed? emissions.
Syntax
Parameters
adjustment    	a GtkAdjustment
lower    	the new minimum value
Since 2.14

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_adjustment_set_page_increment ----
gtk_adjustment_set_page_increment 
Sets the page increment of the adjustment.See gtk_adjustment_set_lower  about how to compress multipleemissions of the ?changed? signal when setting multiple adjustmentproperties.
Syntax
Parameters
adjustment    	a GtkAdjustment
page_increment    	the new page increment
Since 2.14

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_adjustment_set_page_size ----
gtk_adjustment_set_page_size 
Sets the page size of the adjustment.See gtk_adjustment_set_lower  about how to compress multipleemissions of the GtkAdjustment::changed signal when setting multiple adjustmentproperties.
Syntax
Parameters
adjustment    	a GtkAdjustment
page_size    	the new page size
Since 2.14

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_adjustment_set_step_increment ----
gtk_adjustment_set_step_increment 
Sets the step increment of the adjustment.See gtk_adjustment_set_lower  about how to compress multipleemissions of the ?changed? signal when setting multiple adjustmentproperties.
Syntax
Parameters
adjustment    	a GtkAdjustment
step_increment    	the new step increment
Since 2.14

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_adjustment_set_upper ----
gtk_adjustment_set_upper 
Sets the maximum value of the adjustment.Note that values will be restricted byupper - page-size if the page-sizeproperty is nonzero.See gtk_adjustment_set_lower  about how to compress multipleemissions of the ?changed? signal when setting multiple adjustmentproperties.
Syntax
Parameters
adjustment    	a GtkAdjustment
upper    	the new maximum value
Since 2.1
------------ KeyGTK3gtk_alignment_new ----
gtk_alignment_new 
Creates a new GtkAlignment.
Syntax
Parameters
xalign    	the horizontal alignment of the child widget, from 0 (left) to 1(right).
yalign    	the vertical alignment of the child widget, from 0 (top) to 1(bottom).
xscale    	the amount that the child widget expands horizontally to fill upunused space, from 0 to 1.A value of 0 indicates that the child widget should never expand.A value of 1 indicates that the child widget will expand to fill all of thespace allocated for the GtkAlignment.
yscale    	the amount that the child widget expands vertically to fill upunused space, from 0 to 1. The values are similar to xscale.
Returns
 the new GtkAlignment.

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_alignment_set ----
gtk_alignment_set 
Sets the GtkAlignment values.
Syntax
Parameters
alignment    	a GtkAlignment.
xalign    	the horizontal alignment of the child widget, from 0 (left) to 1(right).
yalign    	the vertical alignment of the child widget, from 0 (top) to 1(bottom).
xscale    	the amount that the child widget expands horizontally to fill upunused space, from 0 to 1.A value of 0 indicates that the child widget should never expand.A value of 1 indicates that the child widget will expand to fill all of thespace allocated for the GtkAlignment.
yscale    	the amount that the child widget expands vertically to fill upunused space, from 0 to 1. The values are similar to xscale.

