------------ KeyGTK3gtk_dialog_set_alternative_button_order ----
gtk_dialog_set_alternative_button_order 
gtk_dialog_set_alternative_button_order has been deprecated since version 3.10 and should not be used in newly-written code.DeprecatedSets an alternative button order. If the?gtk-alternative-button-order? setting is set to TRUE,the dialog buttons are reordered according to the order of theresponse ids passed to this function.By default, GTK+ dialogs use the button order advocated by theGNOME Human Interface Guidelineswith the affirmative button at the farright, and the cancel button left of it. But the builtin GTK+ dialogsand GtkMessageDialogs do provide an alternative button order,which is more suitable on some platforms, e.g. Windows.Use this function after adding all the buttons to your dialog, as thefollowing example shows:                    12345678910111213141516171819[/syntax]        [syntax]cancel_button = gtk_dialog_add_button (GTK_DIALOG (dialog),                                       _("_Cancel"),                                       GTK_RESPONSE_CANCEL);ok_button = gtk_dialog_add_button (GTK_DIALOG (dialog),                                   _("_OK"),                                   GTK_RESPONSE_OK);gtk_widget_grab_default (ok_button);help_button = gtk_dialog_add_button (GTK_DIALOG (dialog),                                     _("_Help"),                                     GTK_RESPONSE_HELP);gtk_dialog_set_alternative_button_order (GTK_DIALOG (dialog),                                         GTK_RESPONSE_OK,                                         GTK_RESPONSE_CANCEL,                                         GTK_RESPONSE_HELP,                                         -1);[/syntax]      
      
Syntax
Parameters
dialog    	a GtkDialog
first_response_id    	a response id used by one dialog?s buttons
...    	a list of more response ids of dialog?s buttons, terminated by -1
Since 2.6

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_dialog_set_alternative_button_order_from_array ----
gtk_dialog_set_alternative_button_order_from_array 
gtk_dialog_set_alternative_button_order_from_array has been deprecated since version 3.10 and should not be used in newly-written code.DeprecatedSets an alternative button order. If the?gtk-alternative-button-order? setting is set to TRUE,the dialog buttons are reordered according to the order of theresponse ids in new_order.See gtk_dialog_set_alternative_button_order  for more information.This function is for use by language bindings.
Syntax
Parameters
dialog    	a GtkDialog
n_params    	the number of response ids in new_order
new_order    	 an array of response ids ofdialog?s buttons. [array length=n_params]
Since 2.
