------------ KeyGTK3gtk_entry_set_invisible_char ----
gtk_entry_set_invisible_char 
Sets the character to use in place of the actual text whengtk_entry_set_visibility  has been called to set text visibilityto FALSE. i.e. this is the character used in ?password mode? toshow the user how many characters have been typed. By default, GTK+picks the best invisible char available in the current font. If youset the invisible char to 0, then the user will get no feedbackat all; there will be no text on the screen as they type.
Syntax
Parameters
entry    	a GtkEntry
ch    	a Unicode character

