------------ KeyGTK3gtk_grid_new ----
gtk_grid_new 
Creates a new grid widget.
Returns
 the new GtkGrid

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_grid_attach ----
gtk_grid_attach 
Adds a widget to the grid.The position of child is determined by left and top. Thenumber of ?cells? that child will occupy is determined bywidth and height.
Syntax
Parameters
grid    	a GtkGrid
child    	the widget to add
left    	the column number to attach the left side of childto
top    	the row number to attach the top side of childto
width    	the number of columns that childwill span
height    	the number of rows that childwill span

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_grid_attach_next_to ----
gtk_grid_attach_next_to 
Adds a widget to the grid.The widget is placed next to sibling, on the side determined byside. When sibling is NULL, the widget is placed in row (forleft or right placement) or column 0 (for top or bottom placement),at the end indicated by side.Attaching widgets labeled [1], [2], [3] with sibling == NULL andside == GTK_POS_LEFT yields a layout of 3[1].
Syntax
Parameters
grid    	a GtkGrid
child    	the widget to add
sibling    	 the child of gridthat childwill be placednext to, or NULL to place childat the beginning or end. [allow-none]
side    	the side of siblingthat childis positioned next to
width    	the number of columns that childwill span
height    	the number of rows that childwill span

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_grid_get_child_at ----
gtk_grid_get_child_at 
Gets the child of grid whose area covers the gridcell whose upper left corner is at left, top.
Syntax
Parameters
grid    	a GtkGrid
left    	the left edge of the cell
top    	the top edge of the cell
Returns
 the child at the given position, or NULL. [transfer none]
Since 3.2

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_grid_insert_row ----
gtk_grid_insert_row 
Inserts a row at the specified position.Children which are attached at or below this positionare moved one row down. Children which span across thisposition are grown to span the new row.
Syntax
Parameters
grid    	a GtkGrid
position    	the position to insert the row at
Since 3.2

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_grid_insert_column ----
gtk_grid_insert_column 
Inserts a column at the specified position.Children which are attached at or to the right of this positionare moved one column to the right. Children which span across thisposition are grown to span the new column.
Syntax
Parameters
grid    	a GtkGrid
position    	the position to insert the column at
Since 3.2

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_grid_remove_row ----
gtk_grid_remove_row 
Removes a row from the grid.Children that are placed in this row are removed,spanning children that overlap this row have theirheight reduced by one, and children below the roware moved up.
Syntax
Parameters
grid    	a GtkGrid
position    	the position of the row to remove
Since 3.10

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_grid_remove_column ----
gtk_grid_remove_column 
Removes a column from the grid.Children that are placed in this column are removed,spanning children that overlap this column have theirwidth reduced by one, and children after the columnare moved to the left.
Syntax
Parameters
grid    	a GtkGrid
position    	the position of the column to remove
Since 3.10

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_grid_insert_next_to ----
gtk_grid_insert_next_to 
Inserts a row or column at the specified position.The new row or column is placed next to sibling, on the sidedetermined by side. If side is GTK_POS_TOP or GTK_POS_BOTTOM,a row is inserted. If side is GTK_POS_LEFT of GTK_POS_RIGHT,a column is inserted.
Syntax
Parameters
grid    	a GtkGrid
sibling    	the child of gridthat the new row or column will beplaced next to
side    	the side of siblingthat childis positioned next to
Since 3.2

