Returns
 a new GtkListStore. [transfer full]

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_list_store_set_column_types ----
gtk_list_store_set_column_types 
This function is meant primarily for GObjects that inherit from GtkListStore,and should only be used when constructing a new GtkListStore.  It will notfunction after a row has been added, or a method on the GtkTreeModelinterface is called.
Syntax
Parameters
list_store    	A GtkListStore
n_columns    	Number of columns for the list store
types    	 An array length n of GTypes. [array length=n_columns]

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_list_store_set ----
gtk_list_store_set 
Sets the value of one or more cells in the row referenced by iter.The variable argument list should contain integer column numbers,each column number followed by the value to be set.The list is terminated by a -1. For example, to set column 0 with typeG_TYPE_STRING to ?Foo?, you would write gtk_list_store_set (store, iter,0, "Foo", -1).The value will be referenced by the store if it is a G_TYPE_OBJECT, and itwill be copied if it is a G_TYPE_STRING or G_TYPE_BOXED.
Syntax
Parameters
list_store    	a GtkListStore
iter    	row iterator
...    	pairs of column number and value, terminated with -1

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_list_store_set_valist ----
gtk_list_store_set_valist 
See gtk_list_store_set ; this version takes a va_list for use by languagebindings.
Syntax
Parameters
list_store    	A GtkListStore
