------------ KeyGTK3gtk_progress_bar_new ----
gtk_progress_bar_new 
Creates a new GtkProgressBar.
Returns
 a GtkProgressBar.

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_progress_bar_pulse ----
gtk_progress_bar_pulse 
Indicates that some progress has been made, but you don?t know how much.Causes the progress bar to enter ?activity mode,? where a blockbounces back and forth. Each call to gtk_progress_bar_pulse causes the block to move by a little bit (the amount of movementper pulse is determined by gtk_progress_bar_set_pulse_step ).
Syntax
Parameters
pbar    	a GtkProgressBar

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_progress_bar_set_fraction ----
gtk_progress_bar_set_fraction 
Causes the progress bar to ?fill in? the given fractionof the bar. The fraction should be between 0.0 and 1.0,inclusive.
Syntax
Parameters
pbar    	a GtkProgressBar
fraction    	fraction of the task that?s been completed

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_progress_bar_get_fraction ----
gtk_progress_bar_get_fraction 
Returns the current fraction of the task that?s been completed.
Syntax
Parameters
pbar    	a GtkProgressBar
Returns
 a fraction from 0.0 to 1.0

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_progress_bar_set_inverted ----
gtk_progress_bar_set_inverted 
Progress bars normally grow from top to bottom or left to right.Inverted progress bars grow in the opposite direction.
Syntax
Parameters
pbar    	a GtkProgressBar
inverted    	TRUE to invert the progress bar

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_progress_bar_get_inverted ----
gtk_progress_bar_get_inverted 
Gets the value set by gtk_progress_bar_set_inverted .
Syntax
Parameters
pbar    	a GtkProgressBar
Returns
 TRUE if the progress bar is inverted

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_progress_bar_set_show_text ----
gtk_progress_bar_set_show_text 
Sets whether the progress bar will show text superimposedover the bar. The shown text is either the value ofthe ?text? property or, if that is NULL,the ?fraction? value, as a percentage.To make a progress bar that is styled and sized suitably for containingtext (even if the actual text is blank), set ?show-text? toTRUE and ?text? to the empty string (not NULL).
Syntax
Parameters
pbar    	a GtkProgressBar
show_text    	whether to show superimposed text
Since 3.0

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_progress_bar_get_show_text ----
gtk_progress_bar_get_show_text 
Gets the value of the ?show-text? property.See gtk_progress_bar_set_show_text .
Syntax
Parameters
pbar    	a GtkProgressBar
Returns
 TRUE if text is shown in the progress bar
Since 3.0

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_progress_bar_set_text ----
gtk_progress_bar_set_text 
Causes the given text to appear superimposed on the progress bar.If text is NULL and ?show-text? is TRUE, the currentvalue of ?fraction? will be displayed as a percentage.If text is non-NULL and ?show-text? is TRUE, the text willbe displayed. In this case, it will not display the progress percentage.If text is the empty string, the progress bar will still be styled and sizedsuitably for containing text, as long as ?show-text? is TRUE.
Syntax
Parameters
pbar    	a GtkProgressBar
text    	 a UTF-8 string, or NULL. [allow-none]

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_progress_bar_get_text ----
gtk_progress_bar_get_text 
Retrieves the text displayed superimposed on the progress bar,if any, otherwise NULL. The return value is a referenceto the text, not a copy of it, so will become invalidif you change the text in the progress bar.
Syntax
Parameters
pbar    	a GtkProgressBar
Returns
 text, or NULL; this string is owned by the widgetand should not be modified or freed.

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_progress_bar_set_ellipsize ----
gtk_progress_bar_set_ellipsize 
Sets the mode used to ellipsize (add an ellipsis: "...") the textif there is not enough space to render the entire string.
Syntax
Parameters
pbar    	a GtkProgressBar
mode    	a PangoEllipsizeMode
Since 2.6

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_progress_bar_get_ellipsize ----
gtk_progress_bar_get_ellipsize 
Returns the ellipsizing position of the progress bar.See gtk_progress_bar_set_ellipsize .
Syntax
Parameters
pbar    	a GtkProgressBar
Returns
