Syntax
Parameters
buffer    	a GtkTextBuffer 
Returns
 TRUE if the there is text selected
Since 2.10

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_text_buffer_place_cursor ----
gtk_text_buffer_place_cursor 
This function moves the ?insert? and ?selection_bound? markssimultaneously.  If you move them to the same place in two stepswith gtk_text_buffer_move_mark , you will temporarily select aregion in between their old and new locations, which can be prettyinefficient since the temporarily-selected region will force stuffto be recalculated. This function moves them as a unit, which canbe optimized.
Syntax
Parameters
buffer    	a GtkTextBuffer
where    	where to put the cursor

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_text_buffer_select_range ----
gtk_text_buffer_select_range 
This function moves the ?insert? and ?selection_bound? markssimultaneously.  If you move them in two stepswith gtk_text_buffer_move_mark , you will temporarily select aregion in between their old and new locations, which can be prettyinefficient since the temporarily-selected region will force stuffto be recalculated. This function moves them as a unit, which canbe optimized.
Syntax
Parameters
buffer    	a GtkTextBuffer
ins    	where to put the ?insert? mark
bound    	where to put the ?selection_bound? mark
Since 2.4

