------------ KeyGTK3gtk_text_iter_get_char ----
gtk_text_iter_get_char 
The Unicode character at this iterator is returned.  (Equivalent tooperator* on a C++ iterator.)  If the element at this iterator is anon-character element, such as an image embedded in the buffer, theUnicode ?unknown? character 0xFFFC is returned. If invoked onthe end iterator, zero is returned; zero is not a valid Unicode character.So you can write a loop which ends when gtk_text_iter_get_char returns 0.
Syntax
Parameters
iter    	an iterator
Returns
 a Unicode character, or 0 if iteris not dereferenceable

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_text_iter_get_slice ----
gtk_text_iter_get_slice 
Returns the text in the given range. A ?slice? is an array ofcharacters encoded in UTF-8 format, including the Unicode ?unknown?character 0xFFFC for iterable non-character elements in the buffer,such as images.  Because images are encoded in the slice, byte andcharacter offsets in the returned array will correspond to byteoffsets in the text buffer. Note that 0xFFFC can occur in normaltext as well, so it is not a reliable indicator that a pixbuf orwidget is in the buffer.
Syntax
Parameters
start    	iterator at start of a range
end    	iterator at end of a range
Returns
 slice of text from the buffer

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_text_iter_get_text ----
gtk_text_iter_get_text 
Returns text in the given range.  If the rangecontains non-text elements such as images, the character and byteoffsets in the returned string will not correspond to character andbyte offsets in the buffer. If you want offsets to correspond, seegtk_text_iter_get_slice .
Syntax
Parameters
start    	iterator at start of a range
end    	iterator at end of a range
Returns
 array of characters from the buffer

