------------ KeyGTK3gtk_tool_item_get_toolbar_style ----
gtk_tool_item_get_toolbar_style 
Returns the toolbar style used for tool_item. Custom subclasses ofGtkToolItem should call this function in the handler of theGtkToolItem::toolbar_reconfigured signal to find out in what stylethe toolbar is displayed and change themselves accordingly Possibilities are:GTK_TOOLBAR_BOTH, meaning the tool item should showboth an icon and a label, stacked verticallyGTK_TOOLBAR_ICONS, meaning the toolbar shows only iconsGTK_TOOLBAR_TEXT, meaning the tool item should only show textGTK_TOOLBAR_BOTH_HORIZ, meaning the tool item should showboth an icon and a label, arranged horizontally
Syntax
Parameters
tool_item    	a GtkToolItem 
Returns
 A GtkToolbarStyle indicating the toolbar style usedfor tool_item.
Since 2.4

