------------ KeyGTK3gtk_tree_sortable_set_sort_column_id ----
gtk_tree_sortable_set_sort_column_id 
Sets the current sort column to be sort_column_id. The sortable willresort itself to reflect this change, after emitting a?sort-column-changed? signal. sort_column_id may either bea regular column id, or one of the following special values:GTK_TREE_SORTABLE_DEFAULT_SORT_COLUMN_ID: the default sort functionwill be used, if it is setGTK_TREE_SORTABLE_UNSORTED_SORT_COLUMN_ID: no sorting will occur
Syntax
Parameters
sortable    	A GtkTreeSortable
sort_column_id    	the sort column id to set
order    	The sort order of the column

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_tree_sortable_set_sort_func ----
gtk_tree_sortable_set_sort_func 
Sets the comparison function used when sorting to be sort_func. If thecurrent sort column id of sortable is the same as sort_column_id, then the model will sort using this function.
Syntax
Parameters
sortable    	A GtkTreeSortable
sort_column_id    	the sort column id to set the function for
sort_func    	The comparison function
user_data    	 User data to pass to sort_func, or NULL. [allow-none]
destroy    	 Destroy notifier of user_data, or NULL. [allow-none]

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_tree_sortable_set_default_sort_func ----
gtk_tree_sortable_set_default_sort_func 
Sets the default comparison function used when sorting to be sort_func.  If the current sort column id of sortable isGTK_TREE_SORTABLE_DEFAULT_SORT_COLUMN_ID, then the model will sort using this function.If sort_func is NULL, then there will be no default comparison function.This means that once the model  has been sorted, it can?t go back to thedefault state. In this case, when the current sort column id of sortable is GTK_TREE_SORTABLE_DEFAULT_SORT_COLUMN_ID, the model will be unsorted.
Syntax
Parameters
sortable    	A GtkTreeSortable
sort_func    	The comparison function
user_data    	 User data to pass to sort_func, or NULL. [allow-none]
destroy    	 Destroy notifier of user_data, or NULL. [allow-none]

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_tree_sortable_has_default_sort_func ----
gtk_tree_sortable_has_default_sort_func 
Returns TRUE if the model has a default sort function. This is usedprimarily by GtkTreeViewColumns in order to determine if a model can go back to the default state, or not.
Syntax
Parameters
sortable    	A GtkTreeSortable
Returns
 TRUE, if the model has a default sort functio
------------ KeyGTK3gtk_tree_store_new ----
gtk_tree_store_new 
Creates a new tree store as with n_columns columns each of the types passedin.  Note that only types derived from standard GObject fundamental typesare supported.As an example, gtk_tree_store_new (3, G_TYPE_INT, G_TYPE_STRING,GDK_TYPE_PIXBUF); will create a new GtkTreeStore with three columns, of typegint, gchararray, and GdkPixbuf respectively.
Syntax
Parameters
n_columns    	number of columns in the tree store
...    	all GType types for the columns, from first to last
Returns
 a new GtkTreeStore

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_tree_store_newv ----
gtk_tree_store_newv 
Non vararg creation function.  Used primarily by language bindings.
Syntax
Parameters
n_columns    	number of columns in the tree store
types    	 an array of GType types for the columns, from first to last. [array length=n_columns]
Returns
 a new GtkTreeStore. [transfer full]

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_tree_store_set_column_types ----
gtk_tree_store_set_column_types 
This function is meant primarily for GObjects that inherit from GtkTreeStore, and should only be used when constructing a new GtkTreeStore.  It will not function after a row has been added, or a method on the GtkTreeModel interface is called.
Syntax
Parameters
tree_store    	A GtkTreeStore
n_columns    	Number of columns for the tree store
types    	 An array of GType types, one for each column. [array length=n_columns]

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_tree_store_set_value ----
gtk_tree_store_set_value 
Sets the data in the cell specified by iter and column.The type of value must be convertible to the type of thecolumn.
Syntax
Parameters
tree_store    	a GtkTreeStore
iter    	A valid GtkTreeIter for the row being modified
column    	column number to modify
value    	new value for the cell

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_tree_store_set ----
gtk_tree_store_set 
Sets the value of one or more cells in the row referenced by iter.The variable argument list should contain integer column numbers,each column number followed by the value to be set.The list is terminated by a -1. For example, to set column 0 with typeG_TYPE_STRING to ?Foo?, you would writegtk_tree_store_set (store, iter, 0, "Foo", -1).The value will be referenced by the store if it is a G_TYPE_OBJECT, and itwill be copied if it is a G_TYPE_STRING or G_TYPE_BOXED.
Syntax
Parameters
tree_store    	A GtkTreeStore
iter    	A valid GtkTreeIter for the row being modified
...    	pairs of column number and value, terminated with -1

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_tree_store_set_valist ----
gtk_tree_store_set_valist 
See gtk_tree_store_set ; this version takes a va_list foruse by language bindings.
Syntax
Parameters
tree_store    	A GtkTreeStore
iter    	A valid GtkTreeIter for the row being modified
var_args    	va_list of column/value pairs

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_tree_store_set_valuesv ----
gtk_tree_store_set_valuesv 
A variant of gtk_tree_store_set_valist  which takesthe columns and values as two arrays, instead of varargs.  Thisfunction is mainly intended for language bindings or in casethe number of columns to change is not known until run-time.
Syntax
Parameters
tree_store    	A GtkTreeStore
iter    	A valid GtkTreeIter for the row being modified
columns    	 an array of column numbers. [array length=n_values]
values    	 an array of GValues. [array length=n_values]
n_values    	the length of the columnsand valuesarrays
Since 2.12

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_tree_store_remove ----
gtk_tree_store_remove 
Removes iter from tree_store.  After being removed, iter is set to thenext valid row at that level, or invalidated if it previously pointed to thelast one.
Syntax
Parameters
tree_store    	A GtkTreeStore
iter    	A valid GtkTreeIter
Returns
 TRUE if iteris still valid, FALSE if not.

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_tree_store_insert ----
gtk_tree_store_insert 
Creates a new row at position.  If parent is non-NULL, then the row will bemade a child of parent.  Otherwise, the row will be created at the toplevel.If position is -1 or is larger than the number of rows at that level, thenthe new row will be inserted to the end of the list.  iter will be changedto point to this new row.  The row will be empty after this function iscalled.  To fill in values, you need to call gtk_tree_store_set  orgtk_tree_store_set_value .
Syntax
Parameters
tree_store    	A GtkTreeStore
iter    	 An unset GtkTreeIter to set to the new row. [out]
parent    	 A valid GtkTreeIter, or NULL. [allow-none]
position    	position to insert the new row, or -1 for last

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_tree_store_insert_before ----
gtk_tree_store_insert_before 
Inserts a new row before sibling.  If sibling is NULL, then the row willbe appended to parent ?s children.  If parent and sibling are NULL, thenthe row will be appended to the toplevel.  If both sibling and parent areset, then parent must be the parent of sibling.  When sibling is set,parent is optional.iter will be changed to point to this new row.  The row will be empty afterthis function is called.  To fill in values, you need to callgtk_tree_store_set  or gtk_tree_store_set_value .
Syntax
Parameters
tree_store    	A GtkTreeStore
iter    	 An unset GtkTreeIter to set to the new row. [out]
parent    	 A valid GtkTreeIter, or NULL. [allow-none]
sibling    	 A valid GtkTreeIter, or NULL. [allow-none]

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_tree_store_insert_after ----
gtk_tree_store_insert_after 
Inserts a new row after sibling.  If sibling is NULL, then the row will beprepended to parent ?s children.  If parent and sibling are NULL, thenthe row will be prepended to the toplevel.  If both sibling and parent areset, then parent must be the parent of sibling.  When sibling is set,parent is optional.iter will be changed to point to this new row.  The row will be empty afterthis function is called.  To fill in values, you need to callgtk_tree_store_set  or gtk_tree_store_set_value .
Syntax
Parameters
tree_store    	A GtkTreeStore
iter    	 An unset GtkTreeIter to set to the new row. [out]
parent    	 A valid GtkTreeIter, or NULL. [allow-none]
sibling    	 A valid GtkTreeIter, or NULL. [allow-none]

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_tree_store_insert_with_values ----
gtk_tree_store_insert_with_values 
Creates a new row at position. iter will be changed to point to thisnew row. If position is -1, or larger than the number of rows on the list, thenthe new row will be appended to the list. The row will be filled withthe values given to this function.Callinggtk_tree_store_insert_with_values (tree_store, iter, position, ...)has the same effect as calling                    12[/syntax]        [syntax]gtk_tree_store_insert (tree_store, iter, position);gtk_tree_store_set (tree_store, iter, ...);[/syntax]      
      with the different that the former will only emit a row_inserted signal,while the latter will emit row_inserted, row_changed and if the tree storeis sorted, rows_reordered.  Since emitting the rows_reordered signalrepeatedly can affect the performance of the program,gtk_tree_store_insert_with_values  should generally be preferred wheninserting rows in a sorted tree store.
Syntax
Parameters
tree_store    	A GtkTreeStore
iter    	 An unset GtkTreeIter to set the new row, or NULL. [out][allow-none]
parent    	 A valid GtkTreeIter, or NULL. [allow-none]
position    	position to insert the new row, or -1 to append after existing rows
...    	pairs of column number and value, terminated with -1
Since 2.10

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_tree_store_insert_with_valuesv ----
gtk_tree_store_insert_with_valuesv 
A variant of gtk_tree_store_insert_with_values  which takesthe columns and values as two arrays, instead of varargs.  Thisfunction is mainly intended for language bindings.
Syntax
Parameters
tree_store    	A GtkTreeStore
iter    	 An unset GtkTreeIter to set the new row, or NULL. [out][allow-none]
parent    	 A valid GtkTreeIter, or NULL. [allow-none]
position    	position to insert the new row, or -1 for last
columns    	 an array of column numbers. [array length=n_values]
values    	 an array of GValues. [array length=n_values]
n_values    	the length of the columnsand valuesarrays
Since 2.10

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_tree_store_prepend ----
gtk_tree_store_prepend 
Prepends a new row to tree_store.  If parent is non-NULL, then it will prependthe new row before the first child of parent, otherwise it will prepend a rowto the top level.  iter will be changed to point to this new row.  The rowwill be empty after this function is called.  To fill in values, you need tocall gtk_tree_store_set  or gtk_tree_store_set_value .
Syntax
Parameters
tree_store    	A GtkTreeStore
iter    	 An unset GtkTreeIter to set to the prepended row. [out]
parent    	 A valid GtkTreeIter, or NULL. [allow-none]

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_tree_store_append ----
gtk_tree_store_append 
Appends a new row to tree_store.  If parent is non-NULL, then it will append thenew row after the last child of parent, otherwise it will append a row tothe top level.  iter will be changed to point to this new row.  The row willbe empty after this function is called.  To fill in values, you need to callgtk_tree_store_set  or gtk_tree_store_set_value .
Syntax
Parameters
tree_store    	A GtkTreeStore
iter    	 An unset GtkTreeIter to set to the appended row. [out]
parent    	 A valid GtkTreeIter, or NULL. [allow-none]

