------------ KeyGTK3gtk_tree_view_set_destroy_count_func ----
gtk_tree_view_set_destroy_count_func 
gtk_tree_view_set_destroy_count_func has been deprecated since version 3.4 and should not be used in newly-written code.Accessibility does not need the function anymore.This function should almost never be used.  It is meant for private use byATK for determining the number of visible children that are removed when theuser collapses a row, or a row is deleted.
Syntax
Parameters
tree_view    	A GtkTreeView
func    	 Function to be called when a view row is destroyed, or NULL. [allow-none]
data    	 User data to be passed to func, or NULL. [allow-none]
destroy    	 Destroy notifier for data, or NULL. [allow-none]

