Returns
 TRUE if widgetis being destroyed

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_widget_destroyed ----
gtk_widget_destroyed 
This function sets *widget_pointer to NULL if widget_pointer !=NULL.  It?s intended to be used as a callback connected to the?destroy? signal of a widget. You connect gtk_widget_destroyed as a signal handler, and pass the address of your widget variableas user data. Then when the widget is destroyed, the variable willbe set to NULL. Useful for example to avoid multiple copiesof the same dialog.
Syntax
Parameters
widget    	a GtkWidget
widget_pointer    	 address of a variable that contains widget. [inout][transfer none]

