------------ KeyGTK3gtk_widget_set_state_flags ----
gtk_widget_set_state_flags 
This function is for use in widget implementations. Turns on flagvalues in the current widget state (insensitive, prelighted, etc.).This function accepts the values GTK_STATE_FLAG_DIR_LTR andGTK_STATE_FLAG_DIR_RTL but ignores them. If you want to set the widget'sdirection, use gtk_widget_set_direction .It is worth mentioning that any other state than GTK_STATE_FLAG_INSENSITIVE,will be propagated down to all non-internal children if widget is aGtkContainer, while GTK_STATE_FLAG_INSENSITIVE itself will be propagateddown to all GtkContainer children by different means than turning on thestate flag down the hierarchy, both gtk_widget_get_state_flags  andgtk_widget_is_sensitive  will make use of these.
Syntax
Parameters
widget    	a GtkWidget
flags    	State flags to turn on
clear    	Whether to clear state before turning on flags
Since 3.0

