window    	a GtkWindow
setting    	whether to destroy windowwith its transient parent

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_window_set_hide_titlebar_when_maximized ----
gtk_window_set_hide_titlebar_when_maximized 
If setting is TRUE, then window will request that it?s titlebarshould be hidden when maximized.This is useful for windows that don?t convey any information otherthan the application name in the titlebar, to put the availablescreen space to better use. If the underlying window system does notsupport the request, the setting will not have any effect.Note that custom titlebars set with gtk_window_set_titlebar  arenot affected by this. The application is in full control of theircontent and visibility anyway.
