application    	 a GtkApplication, or NULL. [allow-none]
Since 3.0

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_window_set_has_user_ref_count ----
gtk_window_set_has_user_ref_count 
Tells GTK+ whether to drop its extra reference to the windowwhen gtk_widget_destroy  is called.This function is only exported for the benefit of languagebindings which may need to keep the window alive until theirwrapper object is garbage collected. There is no justificationfor ever calling this function in an application.
Syntax
Parameters
window    	a GtkWindow
setting    	the new value
Since 3.0

------------ KeyGTK3gtk_window_set_titlebar ----
gtk_window_set_titlebar 
Sets a custom titlebar for window.If you set a custom titlebar, GTK+ will do its best to convincethe window manager not to put its own titlebar on the window.Depending on the system, this function may not work for a windowthat is already visible, so you set the titlebar before callinggtk_widget_show .
Syntax
Parameters
window    	a GtkWindow
titlebar    	 the widget to use as titlebar. [allow-none]
Since 3.1
